    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0528" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg404"/>

                <head>No. 225.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Noyes</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 17,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>It is indicated to me that there are impediments to entry of pork products
                    shipped before the date of prohibitory decree. Insist energetically that all
                    shipments made before date of decree shall be received on proper inspection, as
                    otherwise great hardship will result to American shippers.</p>
                <closer><signed>BLAINE, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
